  "context": "## Distributed Tiger Teams VS Freelancer Swarms\nDistributed work is not defined by distance. The decisive distinction is whether accountability, context and operational truth remain integrated across the team.\n\nThe Distributed American Innovation account provides an operating setting for work across regions. Define the shared mission, the recipient’s constraints and the route for resolving an exception. Moving a task without its evidence and decision conditions merely relocates coordination work.\n\nLong before 2020, distributed teams already existed in several forms. Some worked on template-based tasks at scale. Some operated as independent high-capability freelancers delivering specialised outputs. Others became fully distributed companies, where entire functions such as teaching, marketing, administration, library management, student coordination or field support operated remotely across locations.\n\nIt was not a marketplace of interchangeable freelancers. It was not a collection of isolated experts delivering separate pieces of work. It was not simply a company allowing remote work.\n\nIt was a high-trust, high-context, high-responsibility operating model designed for frontier operations integration.\nTags: Authority, permissions and delegation 6.67%; Minimum control and sufficiency 6.67%; Decisions and responsibility 23.33%; Business and management 23.33%; Evidence, provenance and attribution 13.33%; Transformation and operational continuity 26.67%\nCard: https://dakleyer.github.io/perspective-beyond/sources/distributed-tiger-teams-vs-freelancer-swarms-n1296/\nSource document: https://jubap.net/distributed-tiger-teams-vs-freelancer-swarms/\n\n",
